{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.FreeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.RingQuot","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.isUnit_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.isUnit_σ","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L263-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σUnit","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L254-L261","doc":"**The generators are units (sorry-free).**  When `q * qi = 1` each\n`σ_i` is a unit of `H_n(q)`, so the braid group maps into `H_n(q)ˣ`\n(the Hecke representation of braids). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σInv_mul_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σInv_mul_σ","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L246-L252","doc":"`σ_i⁻¹ · σ_i = 1` when `q * qi = 1` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_mul_σInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_mul_σInv","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L238-L244","doc":"`σ_i · σ_i⁻¹ = 1` when `q * qi = 1` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σInv","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L233-L236","doc":"The explicit inverse of a generator: `σ_i⁻¹ = σ_i - (q - qi)·1`, read\noff `σ_i(σ_i - (q - qi)) = q·qi = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_quadratic_qou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_quadratic_qou","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L225-L231","doc":"**Skein / canonical QOU form of the quadratic relation:**\nwhen `q * qi = 1`, `σ_i² = (q - qi)·σ_i + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.hom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.hom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L198-L210","doc":"**Universal property (uniqueness).**  Two algebra maps out of\n`H_n(q)` that agree on every generator `σ_i` are equal.  Combined with\n`lift`/`lift_σ`, this exhibits `H_n(q)` as the algebra presented by the\ngenerators `σ_i` modulo the Hecke relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.lift_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.lift_σ","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L183-L196","doc":"**Universal property (computation rule).**  `lift` sends `σ_i` to\n`g i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.lift","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L170-L181","doc":"**Universal property (existence).**  Given a family `g : Fin n → A`\nof images satisfying the three Hecke relations, there is an algebra\nmap `H_n(q) →ₐ[K] A` sending each generator `σ_i` to `g i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.lift_respects","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.lift_respects","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L146-L168","doc":"The free-algebra map `FreeAlgebra.lift K g` respects the Hecke\nrelations, provided the images `g i` satisfy them.  This is the\n`RingQuot.liftAlgHom` side condition, extracted so both `lift` and\n`lift_σ` can name it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_quadratic_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_quadratic_factored","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L120-L131","doc":"The quadratic relation in factored form: `(σ_i - q)(σ_i + qi) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_commute","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L113-L118","doc":"**The commutation relation holds in `H` (sorry-free):**\n`σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `j + 2 ≤ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_braid","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L105-L111","doc":"**The braid relation holds in `H` (sorry-free):**\n`σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**The quadratic relation holds in `H` (sorry-free):**\n`σ_i² = (q - qi)·σ_i + (q·qi)·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.σ","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L95-L96","doc":"The generator `σ_i ∈ H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.mk","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The canonical algebra map from the free algebra onto `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.instAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.instAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L88-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.instRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke.instRing","kind":"instance","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Hecke","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L77-L79","doc":"The **Iwahori–Hecke algebra** `H_n(q)` of type `A_{n-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel.commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel.commute","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L72-L75","doc":"`σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i - j| ≥ 2` (stated for `j + 2 ≤ i`; the\ngenerated congruence is symmetric). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel.braid","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L67-L71","doc":"`σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel.quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel.quadratic","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L64-L66","doc":"`σ_i² = (q - qi)·σ_i + (q·qi)·1` (⇔ `(σ_i - q)(σ_i + qi) = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRel","kind":"inductive","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeAlgebra.lean#L59-L75","doc":"The defining relations of the type-`A_{n-1}` Iwahori–Hecke algebra on\n`n` generators `σ_0, …, σ_{n-1}`, as a `RingQuot` relation on\n`FreeAlgebra K (Fin n)`.  `qi` is the intended inverse of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}